# floor_work_offset.cam — the datum selection, one word (DECISIONS.md "work
# offsets…", forks 1A/4A). `work_offset G55` SELECTS which pre-defined
# machine register this program's coordinate space rides — vise two of a
# two-vise setup, say — and the golden differs from its undeclared twin by
# exactly the G55 in the setup line. Nothing else CAN move: every feature,
# certificate, and stamp gauges the program's own space unchanged; where
# the operator PUT G55 is the setup sheet's business. Setting a datum from
# program text (G92/G10/G52) rejects by name — that act is work
# positioning wearing offset clothes, the conflation tenet 5 forbids.
work_offset G55

units mm
feed 800
plunge 300
rapid_z 5
clearance_z 25
spindle 3000

stock Box(w=60, l=60, h=20, x=0, y=0, z=0)

tool T1 Endmill(dia=10.0)

feature Top Plane(z=-0.5)

run End(tool=T1, surface=Top, stepover=6.0)
